Z||000009||MikeSchaefer||12-06-2001||12:27 AM||||I bought those generic Best Buy 6x9 boxes, painted them up and put them behind the headrests in my 84.  They look awesome and work great, no mods necessary the seat sitting against them keeps em in place.  Here are some friggin huge pics:<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.soulshadow.com/int2.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.soulshadow.com/int11headline.jpg"> <BR>or you could mount one between the seats like I did (although I must admit it doesn't make a whole lot of sense)<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.soulshadow.com/int5.jpg"> <BR>There are even more pics of my car at: <A HREF="http://www.soulshadow.com/myride.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.soulshadow.com/myride.html</A> <BR>It's very easy to do this to any Fiero btw (I've done it to all three of mine and a friends)<BR>Good Luck,<BR>Mike Schaefer <A HREF="http://surf.to/fiero" TARGET=_blank>http://surf.to/fiero</A> ||||reg||6
